
 # Basics - Writing Data

   Query and What it does :-

   Add a row ->
   INSERT INTO orders (id, amount, status) VALUES (1, 500, 'PENDING');

   Modify existing rows (ALWAYS use WHERE, or you update the whole table)->
   UPDATE orders SET status = 'PAID' WHERE id = 1;

   Remove rows (ALWAYS use WHERE)->
   DELETE FROM orders WHERE id = 1;

   Wipe all rows instantly, resets auto-increment — no WHERE clause possible, can't be rolled back on most engines ->
   TRUNCATE TABLE orders;


